          "text": "The task matches the `host-authority-boundary` route in `agent-quickstart.json` exactly (its `required_additional_reads` is empty and no check command is named), so I use only that route.\n\n## Determining Host authority of a newly compiled WAsmC module\n\n**Decision:** Inspect every generated import **before instantiation** and compare each import's **module, name, kind, and signature** against an application-owned exact allowlist.\n\n**How to do it (JavaScript embedding):**\n\n1. `compile(source)` — compile the smallest complete source.\n2. `inspectWasm(bytes)` — enumerate all generated imports of the produced module.\n3. `WebAssembly.instantiate(inspected.module, approvedImports)` — instantiate only with the exact import object your allowlist approves.\n\n**Pure programs:** require `imports=[]` and instantiate with `{}`.\n\n**Key principle:** A declared import is an effect request only. It grants **no** actual authority by itself.\n\n**What must NOT be invented (ambient or private capabilities that are never granted):**\n\n- Ambient filesystem, network, clock, or randomness access\n- Credentials, process, or device access\n- Private handles, transfer plans, Store nonces, or lifecycle helpers (never expose these in application source)\n- JSON used as a WIT replacement\n\nAny import not on your exact allowlist means you stop and do not instantiate — you never broaden a successful task into granting unrequested capabilities, and you keep Host adapters bounded with explicit failure, cancellation, and resource cleanup.",
